{"name":"Monstera Deliciosa","hex":"#75bf0a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"monstera","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the plants of the genus Monstera, known for their holey leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monstera"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monstera deliciosa","blocks":[{"text":"Monstera deliciosa, the Swiss cheese plant or split-leaf philodendron, is a species of flowering plant. The common name \"Swiss cheese plant\" is also used for the related species from the same genus, Monstera adansonii. The common name \"split-leaf philodendron\" is also used for the species Philodendron bipinnatifidum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Monstera_deliciosa2.jpg/330px-Monstera_deliciosa2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monstera_deliciosa","wikidata":"Q161077"},{"title":"Monstera","blocks":[{"text":"Monstera is a genus of 59 species of flowering plants in the arum family, Araceae, native to tropical regions of central and south America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Starr_080731-9572_Monstera_deliciosa.jpg/330px-Starr_080731-9572_Monstera_deliciosa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monstera","wikidata":"Q159216"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Costela-de-ad%C3%A3o%2C_Monstera_deliciosa%2C_em_Bag%C3%A9-RS%2C_Brasil_-_55401301647.jpg/500px-Costela-de-ad%C3%A3o%2C_Monstera_deliciosa%2C_em_Bag%C3%A9-RS%2C_Brasil_-_55401301647.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Costela-de-ad%C3%A3o%2C_Monstera_deliciosa%2C_em_Bag%C3%A9-RS%2C_Brasil_-_55401301647.jpg/1280px-Costela-de-ad%C3%A3o%2C_Monstera_deliciosa%2C_em_Bag%C3%A9-RS%2C_Brasil_-_55401301647.j